      en: "Osogovo Peak (Macedonian: Осоговска Планина) is the highest summit of the Osogovo Mountains at 2,252 m, located in eastern North Macedonia on the border with Bulgaria. The range is composed of Precambrian gneisses and garnets, among the oldest rocks in the region. The peak is part of the transboundary Osogovo Biosphere Reserve. Vegetation includes subalpine forests of pine and beech, as well as alpine meadows with endemic species such as the Osogovo forget-me-not. Historically, the mountains were known for gold and silver mining. The summit offers expansive views over the Kumanovo plain and the Bulgarian town of Kyustendil.",
